{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 8 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nMr. Chanek has an integer represented by a string $$$s$$$. Zero or more digits have been erased and are denoted by the character _. There are also zero or more digits marked by the character X, meaning they're the same digit.Mr. Chanek wants to count the number of possible integer $$$s$$$, where $$$s$$$ is divisible by $$$25$$$. Of course, $$$s$$$ must not contain any leading zero. He can replace the character _ with any digit. He can also replace the character X with any digit, but it must be the same for every character X.As a note, a leading zero is any 0 digit that comes before the first nonzero digit in a number string in positional notation. For example, 0025 has two leading zeroes. An exception is the integer zero, (0 has no leading zero, but 0000 has three leading zeroes).\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 8 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        FastReader input = new FastReader();\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        int T = 1;\n        while (T-- > 0) {\n            String s = input.next();\n            if (s.length() == 1) {\n                char c = s.charAt(0);\n                if (c == '0' || c == '_' || c == 'X') {\n                    out.println(1);\n                } else {\n                    out.println(0);\n                }\n            } else {\n                boolean hasX = false;\n                for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {\n                    if (s.charAt(i) == 'X') {\n                        hasX = true;\n                        break;\n                    }\n                }\n                if (!hasX) {\n                    out.println(computeValue(s));\n                } else {\n                    int total = 0;\n                    for (int digit = 0; digit < 10; digit++) {\n                        char[] chars = s.toCharArray();\n                        for (int j = 0; j < chars.length; j++) {\n                            if (chars[j] == 'X') {\n                                chars[j] = (char) ('0' + digit);\n                            }\n                        }\n                        total += computeValue(new String(chars));\n                    }\n                    out.println(total);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    public static int computeValue(String s) {\n        int n = s.length();\n        int ways = 0;\n        if (s.charAt(0) != '0') {\n            ways = 1;\n        }\n        for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {\n            if (s.charAt(i) == '_') {\n                if (i == 0) {\n                    ways *= 9;\n                } else {\n                    ways *= 10;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        int divisibleBy25Ways = 0;\n        char last = s.charAt(n - 1);\n        char secondLast = s.charAt(n - 2);\n        if (last == '_' && secondLast == '_') {\n            divisibleBy25Ways = 4;\n        } else if (last == '_') {\n            if (secondLast == '0' || secondLast == '5' || secondLast == '2' || secondLast == '7') {\n                divisibleBy25Ways = 1;\n            }\n        } else if (secondLast == '_') {\n            if (last == '0' || last == '5') {\n                divisibleBy25Ways = 2;\n            }\n        } else {\n            int lastTwo = Integer.parseInt(s.substring(n - 2));\n            if (lastTwo % 25 == 0) {\n                divisibleBy25Ways = 1;\n            }\n        }\n        return ways * divisibleBy25Ways;\n    }\n\n    static class FastReader {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public FastReader() {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        }\n\n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n\n        String nextLine() {\n            String str = \"\";\n            try {\n                str = br.readLine();\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                e.printStackTrace();\n            }\n            return str;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        FastReader input = new FastReader();\n        PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        int T = 1;\n        while (T-- > 0) {\n            String s = input.next();\n            out.println(solve(s));\n        }\n        out.close();\n    }\n\n    public static long solve(String s) {\n        int n = s.length();\n        \n        // Check for leading zero issues\n        if (s.charAt(0) == '0' && n > 1) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n        \n        // Check if there are X characters\n        boolean hasX = false;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (s.charAt(i) == 'X') {\n                hasX = true;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        if (!hasX) {\n            return countValid(s);\n        } else {\n            long total = 0;\n            for (int digit = 0; digit < 10; digit++) {\n                char[] chars = s.toCharArray();\n                for (int j = 0; j < chars.length; j++) {\n                    if (chars[j] == 'X') {\n                        chars[j] = (char) ('0' + digit);\n                    }\n                }\n                total += countValid(new String(chars));\n            }\n            return total;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    public static long countValid(String s) {\n        int n = s.length();\n        \n        // If the string starts with '0' and has length > 1, it's invalid\n        if (s.charAt(0) == '0' && n > 1) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n        \n        // Count ways to fill underscores\n        long ways = 1;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if (s.charAt(i) == '_') {\n                if (i == 0) {\n                    // First digit can't be 0\n                    ways *= 9;\n                } else {\n                    ways *= 10;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Check last two digits for divisibility by 25\n        char last = s.charAt(n - 1);\n        char secondLast = s.charAt(n - 2);\n        \n        int divisibleWays = 0;\n        \n        if (last == '_' && secondLast == '_') {\n            // Both last two digits are unknown\n            // Valid endings: 00, 25, 50, 75\n            divisibleWays = 4;\n        } else if (last == '_') {\n            // Only last digit is unknown\n            if (secondLast == '0') {\n                // If second last is 0, last must be 0\n                divisibleWays = 1;\n            } else if (secondLast == '5') {\n                // If second last is 5, last must be 0 or 5\n                divisibleWays = 2;\n            } else if (secondLast == '2' || secondLast == '7') {\n                // If second last is 2 or 7, last must be 5\n                divisibleWays = 1;\n            } else {\n                divisibleWays = 0;\n            }\n        } else if (secondLast == '_') {\n            // Only second last digit is unknown\n            if (last == '0') {\n                // If last is 0, second last can be 0, 2, 5, 7\n                divisibleWays = 4;\n            } else if (last == '5') {\n                // If last is 5, second last can be 2 or 7\n                divisibleWays = 2;\n            } else {\n                divisibleWays = 0;\n            }\n        } else {\n            // No underscores in last two positions\n            int lastTwo = (secondLast - '0') * 10 + (last - '0');\n            divisibleWays = (lastTwo % 25 == 0) ? 1 : 0;\n        }\n        \n        return ways * divisibleWays;\n    }\n\n    static class FastReader {\n        BufferedReader br;\n        StringTokenizer st;\n\n        public FastReader() {\n            br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        }\n\n        String next() {\n            while (st == null || !st.hasMoreElements()) {\n                try {\n                    st = new StringTokenizer(br.readLine());\n                } catch (IOException e) {\n                    e.printStackTrace();\n                }\n            }\n            return st.nextToken();\n        }\n\n        int nextInt() {\n            return Integer.parseInt(next());\n        }\n\n        long nextLong() {\n            return Long.parseLong(next());\n        }\n\n        double nextDouble() {\n            return Double.parseDouble(next());\n        }\n\n        String nextLine() {\n            String str = \"\";\n            try {\n                str = br.readLine();\n            } catch (IOException e) {\n                e.printStackTrace();\n            }\n            return str;\n        }\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.145764938177308e-06, -6.639736966462806e-05, -3.2186455882765586e-06, 0.0, -2.5987286790041253e-05, -4.100715523236431e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -7.152531907195225e-06, -0.00033408781746402383, -1.9550132492440753e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -3.194758028257638e-05, -4.291525328881107e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -4.291525328881107e-06, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -3.504691630951129e-05, -7.152531907195225e-06, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, -2.50339189733495e-06, -1.549708758830093e-05, -4.172316494077677e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -6.198863957251888e-06, -5.245195097813848e-06, -5.483612312673358e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00033802041434682906, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.062299427052494e-05, -1.3232143828645349e-05, -2.8729025871143676e-05, -8.22540732769994e-06, -7.4741430580616e-05, -0.008620903827250004, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -4.768360213347478e-06, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, -1.3947389561508317e-05, -0.00011395759065635502, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -9.536738616588991e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -8.582700684200972e-05, -5.447716102935374e-05, -0.029757937416434288, -0.501293420791626, -